<template><div><section class="section-y bg-ink text-bone"><div class="wrap max-w-4xl"><p class="label-mono text-mint">Operations · 6 min read</p><h1 class="type-page-hero mt-4 font-display leading-[.96] tracking-[-.05em]">The 12-week report is a business risk.</h1></div></section><article class="section-y"><div class="wrap max-w-3xl space-y-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-ink/70"><p>Inspection data loses value every day it sits in a queue. Corrosion does not pause while a PDF is assembled.</p><h2 class="font-display text-[30px] text-ink">Measure the decision, not the deliverable</h2><p>The useful metric is time from run to a signed work list. Everything else — file format, analyst queue, vendor handoff — is overhead.</p><p>Vomtek screens on ingestion and gives the engineer a ranked list. The report becomes a record of the decision, not the decision itself.</p></div></article></div></template>
